<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><title>PGWP Retainer Agreement</title></head>
<body>
<h1>Post-Graduation Work Permit (PGWP) Retainer Agreement</h1>
<p><strong>Date:</strong> {{date}}</p>

<h2>Parties</h2>
<p>This retainer agreement is entered into between the immigration consulting firm
(<strong>Firm ID:</strong> {{firmId}}) and the client:</p>
<p><strong>Client Name:</strong> {{studentName}}<br>
<strong>Client Email:</strong> {{studentEmail}}</p>

<h2>Scope of Services</h2>
<p>The firm agrees to provide the following services in connection with the client's
Post-Graduation Work Permit application:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Eligibility assessment for PGWP under IRCC R200(3)(e)</li>
  <li>Preparation of IMM 5710 and supporting documentation</li>
  <li>Verification of DLI designation status of the client's institution</li>
  <li>Submission via IRCC Online Portal</li>
  <li>Bridging open work permit (BOWP) advice if applicable</li>
  <li>Post-submission follow-up until a decision is received</li>
</ul>

<p><strong>Graduation Date:</strong> {{graduationDate}}</p>
<p><strong>Degree / Program Completed:</strong> {{degreeCompleted}}</p>
<p><strong>Institution:</strong> {{institution}}</p>

<h2>Fees</h2>
<p><strong>Professional Fee:</strong> {{professionalFee}} CAD</p>
<p><strong>Government Processing Fee:</strong> {{governmentFee}} CAD</p>
<p>Fees are held in the firm's client trust account until earned.</p>

<h2>Terms</h2>
<ol>
  <li>The client must apply within 180 days of receiving their final marks.</li>
  <li>The firm is not responsible for processing times set by IRCC.</li>
  <li>Professional fees are non-refundable once preparation has begun.</li>
  <li>This agreement is governed by the laws of Canada.</li>
</ol>

<h2>Signature</h2>
<p>By signing below, the client agrees to the terms of this retainer agreement.</p>
<div class="signature-area">
  <p>Client Signature: ______________________________</p>
  <p>Date: ______________________________</p>
</div>
</body>
</html>
